{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024217-entanglements-chargen-add-on-system-for-mage","id":1024217,"title":"Entanglements Chargen Add-on System for Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-30T04:26:05-08:00","id":1024217,"title":"Entanglements Chargen Add-on System for Mage","content":"So, one of my little side projects is to try to hack the Entanglements system (based off the Smallville RPG Pathways Map) into Chronicles of Darkness game lines. At this point, I've put together a loose structure for how I'd do it:<br /> <br /> 1) Divide the Map into different sections to give clear cues that the game offers different areas of possible focus.<br /> 2) Emphasize some of the fluff-centric parts of CofD chargen, instead of trying to replace it altogether. I.e., worry less about making it mechanically relevant.<br /> 3) Provide gameline-specific phases to guide the process, giving a sense of how to flesh out your character conceptually.<br /> <br /> Here's the Entanglements system: <a href=\"https://yarukizerogames.com/2011/07/17/entanglements/\" target=\"_blank\">https://yarukizerogames.com/2011/07/17/entanglements/</a> I take no credit for it; it's something other people pointed me to. It needs to be read to understand what I'm going for here.<br /> <br /> And here's what I've got for Mage.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instructions</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Go here for the Entanglements PDF: </span></span><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><a href=\"https://yarukizerogames.com/2011/07/17/entanglements/\" target=\"_blank\">https://yarukizerogames.com/2011/07/17/entanglements/</a></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Take a large piece of paper and divide it into the following sections: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sleeper, Shadow, Supernal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sleeper section talks about a Mage\u2019s mortal life: the people and places he knows, cares about, or could exploit. He might hold down a steady job, or simply have waystations that ground him just a little bit. An arrogant Mage probably doesn\u2019t have much here.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Shadow section talks about a Mage\u2019s mystical life: the other Mages he\u2019s in contact with, who he\u2019s working with, who he\u2019s working against. An apostate probably doesn\u2019t bother much with this section.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Supernal section talks about a Mage\u2019s mysterious life: the crazy things that he cares about, the obsessions and addictions that fill his time, the intrusions upon his life by the Abyss and his Peripheral Sight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rank these sections in order.</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The purpose of this ranking is to give the player a way to express their preference for one section over another. This should help weight each section and make it so that the general area of focus (versus, say, a source for out-of-context problems) is clear to everyone at the table.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add one node to the Pathway Map for each player representing their character.</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(The Storyteller shouldn\u2019t contribute to the map directly; instead, he should add new elements after the map is completed.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Step through the following Phases. For each Phase, answer the prompt and add a node to the Pathway Map in the section specified by the Phase.</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">QUIESCENCE: What was your Sleeper life like before the Awakening? How did you react to supernatural things that you noticed?</span></span><ul><li>Sleeper:</li> <li>Rank 2 section:</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">INSPIRATION: Describe your Awakening. Choose your Path. What didn\u2019t make sense, even afterwards?</span></span><ul><li>Supernal:</li> <li>Rank 1 section:</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">INITIATION: Choose a Shadow Name. Consider which Order to join. What duties and obligations do you owe to who? How do you feel about those?</span></span><ul><li>Shadow:</li> <li>Rank 3 section:</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WISDOM: Talk about your Nimbus. How does it affect your friends, family, coworkers, and other Sleeper connections?</span></span><ul><li>Sleeper or Shadow:</li> <li>Rank 1 section:</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OBSESSION: What do you spend all of your spare time working towards? Are you building your own Legacy? Preparing for an expedition? Changing hearts and minds, opening eyes?</span></span><ul><li>Wildcard:</li> <li>Rank 2 section:</li> </ul><br /> ---<br /> <br /> I know that it's restrictive: any kind of extra system like this is going to do that. I hope that I've been able to leave it open enough that the vast majority of concepts would make it through fine. But part of the purpose of this is to get players riffing off each other in order to create things like Touchstones and shared connections, so the idea of the funnel is that you get them to bump up against each other.<br /> <br /> Feedback of any kind? I have yet to have a chance to playtest this, so it's pretty up-in-the-air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:40:22-08:00","id":1024223,"title":"","content":"Well I an new to the nWoD/CoD but I do something similar to this in the fashion of questions and answers, but that is after the character generation. I can see where this is meant to be before and during the character generation to help guide that process. I am setting up a new PBP game and I might see how this fits into that process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}